---
/**
 * Facts: why trust it? The home page's proof band (strategy 0.8: "hero light,
 * proof band dark").
 *
 * A DARK band. Four benefits in hairline columns with gradient icon tiles,
 * each one something the visitor GETS, not a spec (owner 2026-10-22 asked
 * whether the old band was effective, and it was not: "4 listings" and
 * "100 MB" are specs, and "stay in Ireland, never used to train AI" overstated
 * the record, since site-facts.json lists the AI processors outside the EU and
 * the training claim was unverified). Every line restates a claim the page
 * already makes and site-facts.json backs: the morning check over the live
 * sources (Faq), the fit reasons and their total (Capabilities), the ways a
 * tender gets in (site-facts M18, the upload limits in Steps), and proof for
 * every claim (Refusal). D288 (2026-10-22): the box was "Start with one email",
 * but production email intake is off, so it now names the three routes that
 * are live. Connecting a document store is on every paid plan, and that note
 * sits on /integrations/#sources, not in this box. Under them the live
 * trust strip, the six badges word for word from TRUST_BADGES (D255), the one
 * canonical list. No security wording is written here.
 *
 * 2026-10-22, owner review (R285-WEB-REVIEW-2026-10-22 items 6 and 8):
 * "Daily", "7 reasons", "1 email" and "Proof" sat in number sized type, two of
 * them not numbers, and "7 reasons" sat beside a line about a score out of 100
 * without saying what the reasons were. Each box now leads with what the
 * visitor gets, in words, at one size (FactsBand `words`), with the figures
 * still read from site-facts.json. The trust strip under the boxes is gone:
 * the footer carries the same six badges on every route, so the home page
 * printed them twice. The heading no longer promises data safety the band no
 * longer shows. /security/ and the footer row carry it.
 */
import Band from './Band.astro';
import FactsBand from './FactsBand.astro';
import { FACTS } from '../../data/site-facts';

const live = FACTS.sources.live.length;
const fitTotal = FACTS.fit_dimensions.dimensions.reduce((a, d) => a + d.points, 0);
const fitCountWord = FACTS.fit_dimensions.count_word;
---

<Band tone="dark" class="ea-proof" labelledby="ea-proof-title">
  <div class="ea-wrap">
    <h2 class="ea-h2 ea-h2--centre" id="ea-proof-title" data-reveal>Find the right work, and answer it with proof.</h2>
    <FactsBand
      words
      facts={[
        { icon: 'search', value: 'New work every morning', label: `Public contracts that suit you, from ${live} official UK and EU listing sites, checked each day.` },
        { icon: 'sliders', value: `A score out of ${fitTotal}`, label: `Each match is scored on ${fitCountWord} things, like your kind of work and where it is, so you see why it suits you.` },
        { icon: 'upload', value: 'Bring your tenders in', label: 'Search live UK and EU notices, upload a pack, or connect SharePoint, OneDrive and Confluence. No setup call needed.' },
        { icon: 'shield', value: 'Proof for every claim', label: 'Each answer shows which of your own documents backs it up.' },
      ]}
    />
  </div>
</Band>
